      },
      "text": "### Concept-Level Bridge: Object Shell → Text Shell"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#011",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:scripting:00-overview, git-history:scripting:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:scripting:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "scripting",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "scripting",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scripting Languages - Taxonomy and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This mapping holds for any typed/object pipeline shell moving to a text stream shell — PowerShell is just the most common instance."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#012",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:scripting:00-overview, git-history:scripting:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:scripting:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "scripting",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "scripting",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scripting Languages - Taxonomy and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Concept | Object Shell (PS) | Text Stream Shell (Bash/Zsh) | Notes |\n|---------|-------------------|------------------------------|-------|\n| Pipeline unit | .NET object | newline-delimited string | Fundamental difference |\n| Property access | `$_.PropertyName` | `awk '{print $3}'` or `cut -f3 -d,` | Parse out of text |\n| Filtering | `Where-Object { $_.Size -gt 100 }` | `awk '$3 > 100'` or `grep` | Text needs positional logic |\n| Sorting | `Sort-Object -Property CPU -Descending` | `sort -k3 -rn` | Column position in text |\n| Formatting | `Select-Object Name, CPU \\| Format-Table` | `column -t` or `printf` | No intrinsic structure |\n| Error channel | Separate error stream (`$ErrorActionPreference`) | stderr (fd 2) / `$?` | Both use separate channels |\n| Exit status | `$LASTEXITCODE` (external) / `$?` (cmdlet, bool) | `$?` (integer, 0=success) | PS `$?` is bool, not int |\n| Null sink | `Out-Null` or `> $null` | `> /dev/null` | Discard pipeline output |\n| Startup profile | `$PROFILE` | `~/.bashrc` / `~/.bash_profile` | Interactive-only by default |\n| Script security gate | `ExecutionPolicy` (RemoteSigned, Bypass) | `chmod +x` + shebang | Unix: file permission model |\n| Structured data | Hashtables, PSCustomObject, .NET types | jq (JSON), awk (CSV), python | No native structured types |\n| Error on failure | `$ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\"` | `set -euo pipefail` | Both \"strict mode\" patterns |\n| Print to stderr | `Write-Error \"msg\"` | `echo \"msg\" >&2` | Redirect to fd 2 |\n| Print without pipeline | `Write-Host \"msg\"` (terminal-only) | `echo \"msg\" >&2` (idiom) | Neither goes into pipeline |\n| Capture output | `$x = Get-Thing` | `x=$(cmd)` | Subshell in bash captures stdout |\n| Time a command | `Measure-Command { Get-Process }` | `time cmd` | |\n| PATH variable | `$env:PATH` | `$PATH` | env: namespace in PS |\n| Temp variables | `$env:TMPDIR` / `$env:TEMP` | `$TMPDIR` / `/tmp` | |\n| Env vars | `$env:FOO = \"bar\"` | `export FOO=bar` | PS scopes to process |"
    },
    {
