      },
      "text": "### The Quoting Shift"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#014",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:scripting:00-overview, git-history:scripting:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:scripting:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "scripting",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "scripting",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scripting Languages - Taxonomy and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Both shells have quoting rules, but the mechanics differ:"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#015",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:scripting:00-overview, git-history:scripting:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:scripting:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "scripting",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "scripting",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scripting Languages - Taxonomy and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nPowerShell quoting:\n  'literal — no $expansion'          → single = literal always\n  \"interpolates $var and $($expr)\"   → double = interpolates\n  ` (backtick)                       → escape character (NOT backslash)\n  @' ... '@                          → here-string (literal)\n  @\" ... \"@                          → here-string (interpolating)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#016",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:scripting:00-overview, git-history:scripting:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:scripting:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "scripting",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "scripting",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scripting Languages - Taxonomy and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Bash quoting:\n  'no $expansion whatsoever'         → single = literal always (same)\n  \"$var expands, \\n escapes\"         → double = interpolates (same idea)\n  \\ (backslash)                      → escape character (different from PS backtick)\n  <<EOF                              → heredoc (interpolating by default)\n  <<'EOF'                            → heredoc (literal, like @' '@)\n  $'tab\\there\\nnewline'             → ANSI-C quoting (bash-only, no PS equiv)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#017",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:scripting:00-overview, git-history:scripting:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "scripting/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:scripting:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "scripting",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "scripting",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scripting Languages - Taxonomy and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The trap: PS uses backtick as escape; Bash uses backslash.\n  PS:    Write-Host \"column1`tcolumn2\"     # tab\n  Bash:  echo -e \"column1\\tcolumn2\"        # tab (echo -e or printf)\n  Both:  printf \"column1\\tcolumn2\\n\"       # portable (printf is both PS and Unix)\n```"
    },
    {
